course: dictionary
lesson: 6058
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a noun (a thing or a person) and also an adjective (a word that describes). The word around it tells you which job it is doing. The word mercenary is a good example.
explain: «"Private military contractor" is the official name for a hired soldier, a mercenary.» Here mercenary is a noun: it names a soldier who is paid to fight. The sentence gives the clue, because a hired soldier is the same as a mercenary.
explain: Mercenary can also be an adjective, which describes a person. Calling someone mercenary means they care only about money, not about being kind or fair. Kings in old stories hired mercenaries to fight their wars, so the word has a history, but today it is often used to criticise people.
fact: Mercenary can be a noun: a mercenary is a soldier who is paid to fight.
fact: Mercenary can be an adjective: a mercenary person cares only about money.
fact: A mercenary fights for any country or group that pays them, not for their own country.
fact: «Hire mercenaries» means to pay soldiers to fight for you.
fact: Calling someone mercenary is a criticism, so it is an unkind thing to say.
exercise: «"Private military contractor" is the official name for a hired soldier, a mercenary.» What is a mercenary? | *A soldier who fights for whoever pays them | A teacher who works in a school | A sailor who loves the sea | A king who rules a country
exercise: Ben says his sister has a mercenary attitude because she only helps when she is paid. What does mercenary mean here? | Very kind and generous | Quiet and shy | *Interested only in money | Brave in battle
exercise: Which phrase means paying soldiers to fight for you? | *Hire mercenaries | Tell a joke | Count to ten | Water the plants
test: In a story, the king hired mercenaries to win his war. Who are the mercenaries? | Farmers who grow wheat | Kings who rule a land | Children who play in the park | *Soldiers who are paid to fight
test: Mia says her uncle is mercenary because he only helps people when he gets money. What does mercenary mean? | Happy to share his cake | Good at drawing | Very brave in battle | *Interested only in money, not in being kind or fair
exam: Which sentence uses mercenary as an adjective? | A mercenary is paid to fight in the war | *The mercenary boss only cared about the money | Hire mercenaries to guard the gate | The mercenaries marched across the field
